<xri version="1.0">

  <description>
    <p>Cosgrove's Cosmos PixInsight script repository</p>
  </description>

  <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.8.0:1.9.9">

    <package
      fileName="AstroColorMixer-0.9.7.11-beta.zip"
      sha1="175ae4592e40ce22d481bd95609cf8c814c01506"
      type="script"
      releaseDate="20260622"
      remove="src/scripts/CosgrovesCosmos/AstroColorMixer.js">

      <title>Astro Color Mixer v0.9.7.11-beta</title>

      <description>
        <p>Astro Color Mixer is a PixInsight script for nonlinear RGB color and luminance refinement in astrophotography.</p>
        <p><b>What's new:</b> Adds a display workspace warning for Windows and macOS systems where PixInsight reports a workspace smaller than Astro Color Mixer's layout target.</p>
        <p>The warning explains that Windows Display Scaling above 100%, Recommended, or Auto can make a 1920 x 1080 screen appear smaller to PixInsight, and points users to Windows Settings &gt; System &gt; Display &gt; Scale. macOS users are pointed to System Settings &gt; Displays.</p>
        <p>This beta also updates the FAQ, About text, and Technical Appendix for display scaling guidance, and packages the Astro Color Mixer menu icon in both the flat PixInsight script icon path and the previous nested path.</p>
        <p>Processing math, masks, probe behavior, histogram and polar plot math, recipes, preview behavior, passes, layout target sizes, and output behavior are unchanged.</p>
        <p>This is a beta release for testing. PixInsight 1.9.4 or newer is recommended; Apple Silicon Mac users should use the ARM64/Apple-Silicon PixInsight build.</p>
      </description>

    </package>

  </platform>

</xri>
